                "description": "The combination of dry fuels, gusty northwest winds up to 25 to 35\nmph, and minimum relative humidity values of 35 to 45 percent in\nthe lower elevations, and 40 to 50 percent across higher\nelevations will contribute to an elevated risk of fire spread\nwithin much of the Hudson Valley, including Warren, Washington,\nSaratoga, Schenectady, Albany, Rensselaer, Greene, Columbia,\nUlster, and Dutchess counties. The lowest relative humidity and\nstrongest wind gusts are expected during the late morning to mid\nafternoon hours on Friday.\n\nUse extra caution if handling any potential ignition sources such\nas machinery or matches, and ensure to properly extinguish or\ndispose of cigarette butts.",
